From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Log buffer/image copy shapes and skip out-of-range copies

STEAMAC-5/D3/D4 (1.9.15, M1 Max, macOS 15.6.1, appid 949230, two crashes):
SIGBUS/SIGSEGV inside AGXMetalG13X under MVKCmdBufferImageCopy<1>::encode,
the copyFromTexture:...toBuffer: call of a vkCmdCopyImageToBuffer, on a vkr
ring thread. Nothing records what was copied: format, texture, level, slice,
region, pitches, buffer length or span. MoltenVK never checks the span
against the Metal buffer: Metal API validation catches it in development,
a release process passes it to the driver.

Before each Metal copy, compute the bytes the copy uses in the buffer
(offset + (depth - 1) * bytes/image + (block rows - 1) * bytes/row + the last
row's bytes, with the depth/stencil aspect adjustments), and check the level,
slice and size against the texture. A copy out of range is logged
("[mvk-copy] <reason> ...", first 16 per process) and not encoded. Every
distinct copy shape (format, texture, level, size, pitches, options, buffer
storage; not origin or offset) is logged once ("[mvk-copy] shape ..."), up
to 128 per process, at any log level, so a crash in the driver can be
matched to the copies the game made. No change to in-range copies.

The crash itself is not reproduced and its copy is not known to be out of
range. Regression: host/moltenvk/repro REPRO_CASE=sentry-5-copy-range: a
128x128 readback checked byte for byte logs its shape; the same copy into a
4 KiB buffer aborted the process before (Metal validation: totalBytesUsed
65536 > length 4096, the span computed here), now it is logged and skipped.

Generated-by: LLM
